(6123785, 900337, 76335, '<td valign="top">I''ve never met a contrail I didn''t love. Great idea for this challenge.<br/> <br/>A ten for you.</td>', 'I''ve never met a contrail I didn''t love. Great idea for this challenge. A ten for you.', '2010-08-08 22:03:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123786, 900672, 76335, '<td valign="top">This is astounding. Subtle indeed. Blink and the joy is gone, blink again, and she''s grown up. I''m no poet. I do like this. A ten for you.</td>', 'This is astounding. Subtle indeed. Blink and the joy is gone, blink again, and she''s grown up. I''m no poet. I do like this. A ten for you.', '2010-08-08 22:03:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123788, 901236, 76335, '<td valign="top">Excellent. The title describes it (whatever "it" is) quite well. <br/> <br/>A ten for you.</td>', 'Excellent. The title describes it (whatever "it" is) quite well.  A ten for you.', '2010-08-08 22:03:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123790, 900391, 50695, '<td valign="top">Perfect example of Minimalism. Flat and dull, but hiding an exquisite world of experience. The difference between this photo and so many other similar photos is infinitessimal, but to me it is glaringly obvious.</td>', 'Perfect example of Minimalism. Flat and dull, but hiding an exquisite world of experience. The difference between this photo and so many other similar photos is infinitessimal, but to me it is glaringly obvious.', '2010-08-08 22:06:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123791, 901235, 50695, '<td valign="top">childlike exploration of secrets, of self. But is it Minimalism? I say yes, because of the black area on top and the white on the bottom, threatening the coherence and understandability of the image, moving the focus away from the hand, and never quite letting you believe that what you see is really there... which of course, it isn''t. It never is.</td>', 'childlike exploration of secrets, of self. But is it Minimalism? I say yes, because of the black area on top and the white on the bottom, threatening the coherence and understandability of the image, moving the focus away from the hand, and never quite letting you believe that what you see is really there... which of course, it isn''t. It never is.', '2010-08-08 22:10:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123793, 901092, 50695, '<td valign="top">excellent example of Minimalism. The black areas form the room that you assume to be there. The sleeping person on the chair is really only there because of the title. Some kind of furniture, another window or french door, barely hinted at. And yet the room comes completely into our minds, particularly the mood of the room, the night, the sleep we sleep in that room.</td>', 'excellent example of Minimalism. The black areas form the room that you assume to be there. The sleeping person on the chair is really only there because of the title. Some kind of furniture, another window or french door, barely hinted at. And yet the room comes completely into our minds, particularly the mood of the room, the night, the sleep we sleep in that room.', '2010-08-08 22:12:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123797, 901097, 50695, '<td valign="top">Great example of how a lot of detail and texture can still be Minimalist. Funny, the patterns of light are almost Expressionist (which Minimalism was reacting against), but they are more meditative than expressive. The vertical line is the assertion of the artist, "I am here." Other vertical lines exist as ghosts throughout, evoked as though by some law of physics by all that horizontal power. The horizontal lines are actually much more fragile than they appear, just as they are not truly parallel. As I said, this image does not express emotion, it is meditative, and any emotion comes from that meditation, perhaps as one sees the horizontal and vertical vying, unable to ever settle, always losing, loss, loss loss.</td>', 'Great example of how a lot of detail and texture can still be Minimalist. Funny, the patterns of light are almost Expressionist (which Minimalism was reacting against), but they are more meditative than expressive. The vertical line is the assertion of the artist, "I am here." Other vertical lines exist as ghosts throughout, evoked as though by some law of physics by all that horizontal power. The horizontal lines are actually much more fragile than they appear, just as they are not truly parallel. As I said, this image does not express emotion, it is meditative, and any emotion comes from that meditation, perhaps as one sees the horizontal and vertical vying, unable to ever settle, always losing, loss, loss loss.', '2010-08-08 22:18:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123805, 901236, 50695, '<td valign="top">Minimalism presents the Symphony. Our conductor, merely a few lines, enthusiastically waves his arms and the musical notes appear like specks of dirt, surrounding us with their dance. Tonight''s composer, J B___, delights us with a new composition, Caprice for Organ. We don''t hear it, of course, merely feel it stirring somewhere beneath our ribs, deep but bright.</td>', 'Minimalism presents the Symphony. Our conductor, merely a few lines, enthusiastically waves his arms and the musical notes appear like specks of dirt, surrounding us with their dance. Tonight''s composer, J B___, delights us with a new composition, Caprice for Organ. We don''t hear it, of course, merely feel it stirring somewhere beneath our ribs, deep but bright.', '2010-08-08 22:22:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123807, 900444, 50695, '<td valign="top">Ah, the soothing Minimalism of blur, allowing the mind to replace the objects the mind thinks it sees. I''ll be honest, I''m a little jaded about off-center compositions and even off-center lensbaby compositions, but that jadedness is the only thing interfering with my immersion in this Deep End of an image.</td>', 'Ah, the soothing Minimalism of blur, allowing the mind to replace the objects the mind thinks it sees. I''ll be honest, I''m a little jaded about off-center compositions and even off-center lensbaby compositions, but that jadedness is the only thing interfering with my immersion in this Deep End of an image.', '2010-08-08 22:24:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123809, 901126, 50695, '<td valign="top">Minimalism refers to painting. Many have chosen to mimic painting in order to achieve it. You have taken the very interesting approach of creating a photographic equivalent of Minimalism. The pressure point on a membrane creates a three dimensional light effect that is exceedingly "photographic" in style, but still Minimalist. It is what I would call three-dimensional Minimalism, or rather a Minimalist third dimension, i.e. the two dimensions of the photograph disturbed only slightly. The Minimalism exists purely in the disturbance.</td>', 'Minimalism refers to painting. Many have chosen to mimic painting in order to achieve it. You have taken the very interesting approach of creating a photographic equivalent of Minimalism. The pressure point on a membrane creates a three dimensional light effect that is exceedingly "photographic" in style, but still Minimalist. It is what I would call three-dimensional Minimalism, or rather a Minimalist third dimension, i.e. the two dimensions of the photograph disturbed only slightly. The Minimalism exists purely in the disturbance.', '2010-08-08 22:28:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123814, 900321, 50695, '<td valign="top">Most people are taking their Minimalism into the realm of pure abstraction, and it does fine there, but that''s not a requirement. Mondrian suggested music and city streets. Here, using the photographic medium, you suggest a history and an environment. Someone wrote this sentiment, perhaps felt it. They are gone but the sentiment remains. You have captured it, but you do so in Minimalist style, having it fade into its environment, but this fading is a form of belonging, so there''s a happiness to this photo. And look how beautifully it fades. I think that''s a good suggestion for a Minimalist piece to make: that an image will only get more beautiful the more it fades, and that the most beautiful thing of all is emptiness, or utter fullness. What''s the difference, after all? To be full of one thing is to be empty of another, and vice versa. Watch as loVe is made REAL.</td>', 'Most people are taking their Minimalism into the realm of pure abstraction, and it does fine there, but that''s not a requirement. Mondrian suggested music and city streets. Here, using the photographic medium, you suggest a history and an environment. Someone wrote this sentiment, perhaps felt it. They are gone but the sentiment remains. You have captured it, but you do so in Minimalist style, having it fade into its environment, but this fading is a form of belonging, so there''s a happiness to this photo. And look how beautifully it fades. I think that''s a good suggestion for a Minimalist piece to make: that an image will only get more beautiful the more it fades, and that the most beautiful thing of all is emptiness, or utter fullness. What''s the difference, after all? To be full of one thing is to be empty of another, and vice versa. Watch as loVe is made REAL.', '2010-08-08 22:33:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123816, 900969, 50695, '<td valign="top">This is lovely. It flies. And your title suggests it is a diaper. Well played. Minimalism shows us the beauty in all things.</td>', 'This is lovely. It flies. And your title suggests it is a diaper. Well played. Minimalism shows us the beauty in all things.', '2010-08-08 22:34:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123819, 901156, 50695, '<td valign="top">I think you should have moved him over even further. I think. Even so, you fooled my first look. I gave you a 7 without having any idea what I was seeing. I love how this image transforms him... into something delicate, elusive, perhaps sexual.</td>', 'I think you should have moved him over even further. I think. Even so, you fooled my first look. I gave you a 7 without having any idea what I was seeing. I love how this image transforms him... into something delicate, elusive, perhaps sexual.', '2010-08-08 22:36:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123834, 900988, 50695, '<td valign="top">I love the title. I don''t know if you coined the word yourself: it is not entirely absent from the Internet but is awfully obscure even so.<br/> <br/>I like it applied to Minimalism. I think that''s a wonderful goal for this movement: to create some sort of basic unit of imagery. This title/concept brings out the strength of your image: its boldness. You''ve risked being too simple, and not original enough, in order to achieve this boldness. I think it works.</td>', 'I love the title. I don''t know if you coined the word yourself: it is not entirely absent from the Internet but is awfully obscure even so. I like it applied to Minimalism. I think that''s a wonderful goal for this movement: to create some sort of basic unit of imagery. This title/concept brings out the strength of your image: its boldness. You''ve risked being too simple, and not original enough, in order to achieve this boldness. I think it works.', '2010-08-08 22:40:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123841, 901188, 50695, '<td valign="top">I think this is much more akin to the Surrealism of Man Ray than to Minimalism. I love the confusion of horizontal and vertical planes, wonderfully disorienting. I''m giving you an 8 for masquerading Surrealism as Minimalism, but I don''t doubt that I love this picture.</td>', 'I think this is much more akin to the Surrealism of Man Ray than to Minimalism. I love the confusion of horizontal and vertical planes, wonderfully disorienting. I''m giving you an 8 for masquerading Surrealism as Minimalism, but I don''t doubt that I love this picture.', '2010-08-08 22:48:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123842, 900454, 50695, '<td valign="top">Minimalism isn''t really about making the subject small. I would say that Minimalism defies having a subject altogether. Even so, the water is so beautifully textured that it creates its own interest, a meditative texture that I feel is appropriate for Minimalism.</td>', 'Minimalism isn''t really about making the subject small. I would say that Minimalism defies having a subject altogether. Even so, the water is so beautifully textured that it creates its own interest, a meditative texture that I feel is appropriate for Minimalism.', '2010-08-08 22:49:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123853, 900690, 50695, '<td valign="top">this doesn''t fit my idea of Minimalism, but it is an exquisite portrait and it at least acknowledges the topic, so 8 from me.</td>', 'this doesn''t fit my idea of Minimalism, but it is an exquisite portrait and it at least acknowledges the topic, so 8 from me.', '2010-08-08 23:04:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123855, 900768, 50695, '<td valign="top">much more akin to German Expressionism than Minimalism, but you still get a 7 for conveying loveliness with minimal detail.</td>', 'much more akin to German Expressionism than Minimalism, but you still get a 7 for conveying loveliness with minimal detail.', '2010-08-08 23:07:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123858, 900503, 50695, '<td valign="top">reminds me of a jar I once knew in Tennessee</td>', 'reminds me of a jar I once knew in Tennessee', '2010-08-08 23:07:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123860, 900647, 50695, '<td valign="top">You''ve gone a long way toward simplifying this into abstraction, which brings you into the neighborhood of Minimalism. Lovely blur and I love the curved hair-thin lines of the fishing poles.</td>', 'You''ve gone a long way toward simplifying this into abstraction, which brings you into the neighborhood of Minimalism. Lovely blur and I love the curved hair-thin lines of the fishing poles.', '2010-08-08 23:10:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123861, 901212, 50695, '<td valign="top">The spiraling composition is pretty standard fare around here, but I like the roughness of the lines and the brute contrast.</td>', 'The spiraling composition is pretty standard fare around here, but I like the roughness of the lines and the brute contrast.', '2010-08-08 23:11:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123863, 900711, 50695, '<td valign="top">too much visual information to match my idea of Minimalism, but I love the photo, and the composition has a Minimalist sort of simplicity, so 8.</td>', 'too much visual information to match my idea of Minimalism, but I love the photo, and the composition has a Minimalist sort of simplicity, so 8.', '2010-08-08 23:12:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123865, 900084, 83313, '<td valign="top">I think this is probably suffering from the same thing in voting as mine is, too much detail. It is still minimal in my opinion, however. Simple shapes and lines. It totally fits.</td>', 'I think this is probably suffering from the same thing in voting as mine is, too much detail. It is still minimal in my opinion, however. Simple shapes and lines. It totally fits.', '2010-08-08 23:14:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123866, 901125, 50695, '<td valign="top">this fits my idea of Minimalism (one of my ideas of Minimalism): visual information degraded into abstraction. Maybe the water is still a little bit too watery...</td>', 'this fits my idea of Minimalism (one of my ideas of Minimalism): visual information degraded into abstraction. Maybe the water is still a little bit too watery...', '2010-08-08 23:15:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123867, 900617, 83313, '<td valign="top">Q is for "Quirky", which is an approach I like.</td>', 'Q is for "Quirky", which is an approach I like.', '2010-08-08 23:16:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123868, 900945, 50695, '<td valign="top">I like how the feet take the place of the fourth dot we''re expecting to see. It is rich with metaphorical possibility. This is a jokey sort of Minimalism, but Minimalism nonetheless. I could almost call Minimalism a "feeling," the feeling of meditative emptiness... being freed of meaning.</td>', 'I like how the feet take the place of the fourth dot we''re expecting to see. It is rich with metaphorical possibility. This is a jokey sort of Minimalism, but Minimalism nonetheless. I could almost call Minimalism a "feeling," the feeling of meditative emptiness... being freed of meaning.', '2010-08-08 23:16:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123869, 901112, 50695, '<td valign="top">this ain''t minimalism but I''m giving you a 7 for being hilarious.</td>', 'this ain''t minimalism but I''m giving you a 7 for being hilarious.', '2010-08-08 23:16:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6123871, 900582, 50695, '<td valign="top">This is a great example of misunderstood Minimalism. It''s about a more mechanized approach after the emotional excesses of abstract expressionism. What might detract from this Minimalism is the dramatic lighting, giving this an almost operatic feeling that is the opposite of Minimalism... and that''s what makes the picture interesting.</td>', 'This is a great example of misunderstood Minimalism. It''s about a more mechanized approach after the emotional excesses of abstract expressionism. What might detract from this Minimalism is the dramatic lighting, giving this an almost operatic feeling that is the opposite of Minimalism... and that''s what makes the picture interesting.', '2010-08-08 23:20:04.000000', NULL, 1),
