(6933628, 901118, 103142, '<td valign="top">Never was sure about the tilt on this one (probably would have liked a little less of a tilt, but I love, absolutely love the luminescence. It''s so soft and it just seems to glow.</td>', 'Never was sure about the tilt on this one (probably would have liked a little less of a tilt, but I love, absolutely love the luminescence. It''s so soft and it just seems to glow.', '2012-12-15 16:03:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(6938128, 900598, 156757, '<td valign="top">I kind of like this photo. One suggestion would be to try taking the shot at different times of day. It would be a little more interesting if there were a lot of dramatic clouds in the sky. Also if your using Photoshop, use the black and white layer mask and adjust the color tones before the b&amp;w conversion. This allows you to adjust the colors of the image as a b&amp;w to make it really pop out and not look so flat. Maybe turn the chair so that it faces to the left, because right now the chair facing right pulls the viewers eye away from the image. Lots of potential here. Good job!<br/> <br/>-Kevin</td>', 'I kind of like this photo. One suggestion would be to try taking the shot at different times of day. It would be a little more interesting if there were a lot of dramatic clouds in the sky. Also if your using Photoshop, use the black and white layer mask and adjust the color tones before the b&w conversion. This allows you to adjust the colors of the image as a b&w to make it really pop out and not look so flat. Maybe turn the chair so that it faces to the left, because right now the chair facing right pulls the viewers eye away from the image. Lots of potential here. Good job! -Kevin', '2012-12-20 12:40:17.000000', NULL, 0),
